# Icon Filter Rendering Updates

When changing any filter or quick-attribute icon asset, color, size, or proportion, audit the whole rendering path before finishing.

## Check The Actual Icon Path

- Confirm the visible icon id first. In listing cards this comes from `listingCardQuickAttributes()` in `src/components/search/searchQuickAttributes.tsx`.
- Do not assume a visually similar icon is the one being rendered. For example, shared-room/plus-one uses `room-shared` and `PlusOneIcon`, not `gender-mixed`.
- Check the source component too. PNG-backed icons may scale internally (`img` classes like `h-full`, `w-full`, `object-contain`, or custom percentages), so wrapper size changes alone may not update the visible result.

## Update All Relevant Contexts

- Mobile listing cards: `SearchListingCard.tsx` plus `quickAttributeGenderIconClass()` in `GenderFilterIcons.tsx`.
- Desktop listing cards: the non-mobile branch of the same helper.
- Mobile map quick filter rail: `MOBILE_MAP_QUICK_FILTERS` and `SearchFilterRail.tsx`.
- Active filter chips and saved-search summaries: `searchActiveFilterChips.ts`, `horizontalBarFilters.ts`, and any icon metadata they import.

## Refresh And Verify

- Keep Tailwind arbitrary size classes as literal strings (for example `size-[8.96px]`) so the build can include them.
- Run `npm run build` after changing icon classes or assets. This refreshes generated CSS/asset hashes and catches missing classes/imports.
- If an icon asset is replaced but the same component caches a processed data URL, ensure the cache key or asset URL changes, or add a versioned cache key.
- Commit and push only the files related to the icon change; exclude unrelated files such as `_tmp_prod_bundle.js`.
